    {
      "type": "updated",
      "source": "wgmods",
      "sourceId": "4322",
      "title": "CHAMPi's Expected Vehicle Values",
      "previous": {
        "modVersion": "2.02.000",
        "wotGameVersion": "2.3.1.3",
        "fileName": "champi.expectedvehiclevalues2_2.02.000_2.3.1.3.zip",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-21T09:02:00.660Z",
        "changeLog": "- fix: a disabled MoE panel no longer removes the WNX panel in battle too\n- fix: playing below tier 5 no longer shows an empty MoE display after entering the map until the first damage is done\n- add: missing preview images for vertical layout and no. #5\n- add: new MoE panel layout #6\n - add: 3 new MoE tokens for custom panel - see tooltip help in custom battle template\n   - cdmgc = colored combined damage as you knew it from EVV #1\n  - moe_np = MoE Nextpercent - shows the next MoE percent goal\n  - moe_npd = MoE Nextpercent Damage- shows the needed damage in the current battle to reach the \ncurrent percent goal\n- mod: some of the MoE layouts got an alternate display mode to display marks requirements"
      },
      "current": {
        "modVersion": "2.03.000",
        "wotGameVersion": "2.4.0.0",
        "fileName": "champi.expectedvehiclevalues2_2.03.000_2.4.0.0.zip",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-02T20:29:37.740Z",
        "changeLog": "fixed an issue that displayed an empty panel (more a little dot) without text in garage if garage panel was deactivated in settings\nfixed an issue where the moe battle panel only displayed \"TODO!\" when moe layout #6 was selected. 🤭\nnew: option to setup an alternate battle panel that can be activated with ALT key (custom mode required!)\nnew: real time template HTML preview for better control (see screenshot)\nnew battle template tokens added:{itdmg}{tdmg}  - icon for track assist and value{ispdmg}{spdmg}  - icon for spot assist and value{istdmg}{stdmg} - icon for stun assist and value\n{iassist}{vassist} - icon for current assist type and value\nmodified settings screen to use tabs to split setting sections into Garage, Battle, WNX, Color, General and also moved some settings from WNX to General section"
      }
    },
